# Release signing for the Play Store — copy to android/key.properties.
#
# android/key.properties and *.jks are gitignored, and MUST stay that way:
# anyone holding the keystore plus these passwords can publish an update
# that Android will install over the real app.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Create the keystore (run this yourself — it asks for passwords, and
#    nobody else should ever type or see them):
#
#      keytool -genkey -v -keystore %USERPROFILE%\nagarva-upload.jks ^
#        -storetype JKS -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 ^
#        -alias nagarva
#
#    Put it OUTSIDE the repo. A keystore inside the working tree is one
#    `git add -f` from being public forever.
#
# 2. Copy this file to android/key.properties and fill in the four values.
#
# 3. Verify before uploading — a debug-signed bundle is rejected by Play,
#    and the whole point of this setup is to find that out here:
#
#      flutter build appbundle --release
#      keytool -printcert -jarfile build/app/outputs/bundle/release/app-release.aab
#
#    The owner must be YOUR CN, not "CN=Android Debug". If key.properties
#    is missing, the bundle build now fails outright rather than quietly
#    producing a debug-signed artifact.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# BACK THIS UP, IN TWO PLACES, TODAY.
#
# Losing the upload keystore is not a small problem: without Play App
# Signing enrolment you cannot ever update the listing again, and even
# with it you need a Google support reset that takes days. Back up the
# .jks file and these passwords to a password manager, and keep a second
# copy offline. This is the single least recoverable thing in the whole
# project.

storePassword=CHANGEME
keyPassword=CHANGEME
keyAlias=nagarva
# Absolute path, outside the repo. Windows: use forward slashes or escape
# the backslashes, e.g. C:/Users/you/nagarva-upload.jks
storeFile=CHANGEME
